cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the code or the derived tables in this repository, please cite the
  article and the archived release.
title: "The Same Corpus, Two Conclusions: replication package"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Laquintana
    given-names: Mirko
  - family-names: Pareschi
    given-names: Remo
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kymki/same-corpus-two-conclusions"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Replication package for "The Same Corpus, Two Conclusions: How Analyst Choices
  Determine Cross-Platform Findings". The paper shows that three routine analyst
  choices (the unit of analysis, the summary measure, and the criterion delimiting
  each subcorpus) can each determine the substantive conclusion drawn about
  platforms. Code is released under the MIT Licence; documentation and derived data
  tables under CC BY 4.0. The raw corpora are not included.
keywords:
  - topic modelling
  - LDA
  - sentiment analysis
  - cross-platform comparison
  - Reddit
  - Telegram
  - The Guardian
  - reproducibility
